# Muse-Glimmer-30B, full fine-tuning at 64K context, the two-node layout: TRAIN_NODES=1 (TP4 x DP2 training) and the
# head node with four TP2 SGLang engines, a smoke of the 5-node muse-glimmer-30b-128k gateway. The first weight push is
# checked against the engines' own load of the snapshot (--check-weight-update-equal): it covers the bridge's Glimmer
# mapping, the gated QKV split and the norms the engines fold. Two DP ranks hold half of the optimizer state each: a
# training GPU peaked at 101 GiB on 64K-token rows here (and at 120.5 GiB on 131K-token rows with the 128k preset on
# two nodes). Otherwise as muse-glimmer-30b-128k, overlay included: ROOTFS, EXTRA_SITE and HF_HOME job variables
# (deploy/abci/overlays/muse-glimmer/README.md).
# Use: qsub -l select=2:mpiprocs=8 -v PRESET=muse-glimmer-30b-64k,ROOTFS=...,EXTRA_SITE=...,HF_HOME=...
#      deploy/abci/tinker_gateway.pbs
# tinker_gateway.pbs reads this file (it never sources it); a non-empty job variable replaces a value here.
GATEWAY_LAUNCHER=examples/tinker/run_qwen3_6_35b_a3b_gateway.py
MODE=full
HF_MODEL=meta-models/Muse-Glimmer-30B
HF_REVISION=a4e59da52a7bc87ae7251dd5545c0dd437c44b68
LAUNCHER_ARGS="--extra-env-vars NCCL_DEBUG=INFO --model-variant glimmer-30b --model-name meta-models/Muse-Glimmer-30B --tp 4 --context-len 65536 --max-tokens-per-gpu 65537 --max-tokens-per-datum 65537 --unit-token-budget 655370 --check-weight-update-equal"
EXTRA_ARGS="--sglang-attention-backend fa3 --sglang-language-model-only --lr 1e-6 --router-policy cache_aware --router-balance-abs-threshold 16 --router-balance-rel-threshold 1.5"
TINKER_SAMPLE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=1800
